{"module":"many-targets","voice":"male","duration":314.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Muchos blancos: comunidades latinas, asiáticas, indígenas e inmigrantes","start":0.0,"end":6.2,"words":[[0.0,0.49],[0.49,1.14],[1.43,2.33],[2.33,2.98],[3.27,4.08],[4.37,5.11],[5.11,5.19],[5.19,6.09]]},{"el":"intro","text":"La misma maquinaria de leyes, turbas y acusaciones falsas se ha dirigido contra muchas comunidades.","start":7.0,"end":14.45,"words":[[7.02,7.18],[7.18,7.58],[7.58,8.3],[8.3,8.46],[8.46,8.95],[9.23,9.71],[9.71,9.79],[9.79,10.67],[10.67,11.15],[11.15,11.31],[11.31,11.39],[11.39,12.04],[12.04,12.52],[12.52,13.0],[13.0,13.96]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Ver el panorama completo construye coaliciones, y las coaliciones aprueban leyes.","start":14.8,"end":20.4,"words":[[14.82,15.03],[15.03,15.17],[15.17,15.74],[15.74,16.3],[16.3,16.93],[16.93,17.77],[18.02,18.09],[18.09,18.3],[18.3,19.07],[19.07,19.63],[19.63,20.05]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Mexicoamericanos","start":20.75,"end":22.82,"words":[[20.79,22.56]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Los historiadores William Carrigan y Clive Webb documentaron al menos 547 linchamientos de mexicanos en Estados Unidos entre 1848 y 1928.","start":23.52,"end":36.96,"words":[[23.58,23.79],[23.79,24.65],[24.65,25.23],[25.23,25.73],[25.73,25.81],[25.81,26.17],[26.17,26.45],[26.45,27.32],[27.32,27.46],[27.46,27.82],[27.82,29.47],[29.47,30.41],[30.41,30.55],[30.55,31.2],[31.2,31.34],[31.34,31.85],[31.85,32.28],[32.28,32.64],[32.64,34.65],[34.65,34.73],[34.73,36.6]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En enero de 1918, Rangers de Texas, soldados y rancheros locales mataron a 15 hombres y niños mexicanos en Porvenir, Texas.","start":37.31,"end":47.99,"words":[[37.33,37.48],[37.48,37.85],[37.85,38.0],[38.0,39.85],[40.11,40.63],[40.63,40.77],[40.77,41.29],[41.55,42.15],[42.15,42.22],[42.22,42.89],[42.89,43.4],[43.4,43.92],[43.92,44.0],[44.0,44.37],[44.37,44.81],[44.81,44.89],[44.89,45.26],[45.26,45.92],[45.92,46.07],[46.07,46.74],[47.0,47.52]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En Mendez v. Westminster (1947), familias mexicoamericanas ganaron un caso contra la segregación escolar en California, siete años antes de Brown v. Board.","start":48.34,"end":60.98,"words":[[48.39,48.53],[48.53,48.95],[48.95,49.16],[49.51,50.28],[50.28,52.31],[52.55,53.11],[53.11,54.23],[54.23,54.72],[54.72,54.86],[54.86,55.14],[55.14,55.56],[55.56,55.7],[55.7,56.46],[56.46,56.95],[56.95,57.09],[57.09,57.86],[58.11,58.46],[58.46,58.74],[58.74,59.09],[59.09,59.23],[59.23,59.57],[59.57,59.78],[60.13,60.55]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 1943, militares atacaron a jóvenes mexicoamericanos en Los Ángeles en los “disturbios de los Zoot Suit”, y la policía arrestó a las víctimas.","start":61.33,"end":72.84,"words":[[61.35,61.5],[61.5,63.59],[63.85,64.52],[64.52,65.11],[65.11,65.19],[65.19,65.71],[65.71,66.9],[66.9,67.05],[67.05,67.27],[67.27,67.79],[67.79,67.94],[67.94,68.17],[68.17,68.91],[68.91,69.06],[69.06,69.28],[69.28,69.58],[69.58,69.95],[70.21,70.29],[70.29,70.44],[70.44,71.03],[71.03,71.48],[71.48,71.55],[71.55,71.78],[71.78,72.45]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 2019, un hombre armado que había publicado sobre una “invasión hispana” mató a 23 personas en un Walmart de El Paso.","start":73.19,"end":82.7,"words":[[73.19,73.35],[73.35,74.68],[74.95,75.11],[75.11,75.5],[75.5,75.97],[75.97,76.13],[76.13,76.52],[76.52,77.22],[77.22,77.62],[77.62,77.85],[77.85,78.48],[78.48,78.95],[78.95,79.26],[79.26,79.34],[79.34,80.12],[80.12,80.75],[80.75,80.91],[80.91,81.06],[81.06,81.61],[81.61,81.77],[81.77,81.93],[81.93,82.32]]},{"el":"s0","text":"(Ver también el módulo sobre las fronteras.)","start":83.05,"end":86.11,"words":[[83.05,83.26],[83.26,83.74],[83.74,83.88],[83.88,84.3],[84.3,84.65],[84.65,84.85],[84.85,85.55]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Asiático-americanos","start":87.01,"end":89.13,"words":[[87.05,88.76]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Inmigrantes chinos fueron masacrados en Los Ángeles (1871) y Rock Springs (1885) y expulsados de Tacoma (1885).","start":89.83,"end":101.52,"words":[[89.84,90.6],[90.6,91.02],[91.02,91.44],[91.44,92.13],[92.13,92.27],[92.27,92.48],[92.48,92.97],[92.97,94.77],[95.02,95.09],[95.09,95.3],[95.3,95.71],[95.71,97.59],[97.83,97.9],[97.9,98.67],[98.67,98.81],[98.81,99.23],[99.23,101.17]]},{"el":"s1","text":"La Ley de Exclusión China (1882) fue la primera ley de EE. UU. que prohibió la entrada de un grupo por su nacionalidad.","start":101.87,"end":111.18,"words":[[101.89,102.03],[102.03,102.24],[102.24,102.37],[102.37,103.07],[103.07,103.42],[103.42,105.15],[105.39,105.6],[105.6,105.74],[105.74,106.23],[106.23,106.44],[106.44,106.57],[106.57,106.78],[107.13,107.34],[107.69,107.82],[107.82,108.31],[108.31,108.45],[108.45,108.94],[108.94,109.07],[109.07,109.21],[109.21,109.56],[109.56,109.77],[109.77,109.91],[109.91,110.81]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Unos 120,000 japoneses-estadounidenses, la mayoría ciudadanos, fueron encarcelados durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial.","start":111.53,"end":120.91,"words":[[111.57,111.84],[111.84,113.73],[113.73,115.42],[115.66,115.8],[115.8,116.34],[116.34,117.08],[117.32,117.72],[117.72,118.54],[118.54,119.01],[119.01,119.14],[119.14,119.62],[119.62,119.89],[119.89,120.43]]},{"el":"s1","text":"En 1982, Vincent Chin fue golpeado hasta la muerte en Detroit por dos trabajadores automotrices blancos que culpaban a Japón de la pérdida de empleos; fueron condenados a libertad condicional y a una multa de $3,000, lo que desató un movimiento nacional por los derechos civiles asiático-americanos.","start":121.26,"end":143.2,"words":[[121.3,121.44],[121.44,123.31],[123.56,124.07],[124.07,124.35],[124.35,124.57],[124.57,125.14],[125.14,125.43],[125.43,125.57],[125.57,126.0],[126.0,126.15],[126.15,126.65],[126.65,126.87],[126.87,127.08],[127.08,127.94],[127.94,128.81],[128.81,129.31],[129.31,129.45],[129.45,130.03],[130.03,130.1],[130.1,130.46],[130.46,130.6],[130.6,130.74],[130.74,131.25],[131.25,131.39],[131.39,131.97],[132.22,132.65],[132.65,133.37],[133.37,133.44],[133.44,134.01],[134.01,134.8],[134.8,134.87],[134.87,134.95],[134.95,135.16],[135.16,135.52],[135.52,135.66],[135.66,137.53],[137.78,137.93],[137.93,138.07],[138.07,138.5],[138.5,138.65],[138.65,139.36],[139.36,139.94],[139.94,140.15],[140.15,140.37],[140.37,140.94],[140.94,141.45],[141.45,142.81]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Después del 11 de septiembre, sijs y estadounidenses del sur de Asia fueron atacados, empezando por el asesinato de Balbir Singh Sodhi en Arizona pocos días después.","start":143.55,"end":153.46,"words":[[143.55,144.01],[144.01,144.2],[144.2,144.46],[144.46,144.59],[144.59,145.31],[145.54,145.79],[145.79,145.86],[145.86,146.83],[146.83,147.03],[147.03,147.22],[147.22,147.35],[147.35,147.61],[147.61,148.0],[148.0,148.59],[148.82,149.4],[149.4,149.6],[149.6,149.73],[149.73,150.31],[150.31,150.44],[150.44,150.83],[150.83,151.09],[151.09,151.35],[151.35,151.48],[151.48,151.94],[151.94,152.26],[152.26,152.59],[152.59,153.11]]},{"el":"s1","text":"De 2020 a 2021, Stop AAPI Hate recibió más de 10,000 reportes de incidentes de odio antiasiático, y en marzo de 2021 un hombre armado mató a ocho personas, seis de ellas mujeres asiáticas, en spas del área de Atlanta.","start":153.81,"end":172.67,"words":[[153.84,153.99],[153.99,154.93],[154.93,155.01],[155.01,156.34],[156.61,156.92],[156.92,157.24],[157.24,157.47],[157.47,158.02],[158.02,158.25],[158.25,158.41],[158.41,159.97],[159.97,160.6],[160.6,160.75],[160.75,161.54],[161.54,161.69],[161.69,162.0],[162.0,163.02],[163.29,163.37],[163.37,163.53],[163.53,163.92],[163.92,164.08],[164.08,165.33],[165.33,165.48],[165.48,165.87],[165.87,166.34],[166.34,166.65],[166.65,166.73],[166.73,167.05],[167.05,167.75],[168.02,168.34],[168.34,168.49],[168.49,168.88],[168.88,169.43],[169.43,170.21],[170.48,170.64],[170.64,170.95],[170.95,171.19],[171.19,171.5],[171.5,171.66],[171.66,172.28]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Pueblos indígenas","start":173.57,"end":175.24,"words":[[173.57,174.22],[174.22,175.06]]},{"el":"s2","text":"No todos los indígenas recibieron la ciudadanía estadounidense hasta 1924, y Arizona y Nuevo México les prohibieron votar hasta 1948.","start":175.94,"end":187.59,"words":[[175.99,176.13],[176.13,176.48],[176.48,176.69],[176.69,177.31],[177.31,178.01],[178.01,178.15],[178.15,178.91],[178.91,179.88],[179.88,180.16],[180.16,182.04],[182.28,182.35],[182.35,182.84],[182.84,182.9],[182.9,183.25],[183.25,183.67],[183.67,183.88],[183.88,184.57],[184.57,184.92],[184.92,185.2],[185.2,187.21]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los internados federales se tratan en el módulo sobre la conquista.","start":187.94,"end":192.12,"words":[[187.96,188.16],[188.16,188.85],[188.85,189.46],[189.46,189.6],[189.6,190.01],[190.01,190.14],[190.14,190.28],[190.28,190.69],[190.69,191.03],[191.03,191.16],[191.16,191.78]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Hoy, las mujeres indígenas americanas y nativas de Alaska enfrentan tasas muy altas de violencia.","start":192.47,"end":199.2,"words":[[192.5,192.72],[192.98,193.2],[193.2,193.72],[193.72,194.38],[194.38,195.12],[195.12,195.19],[195.19,195.71],[195.71,195.85],[195.85,196.3],[196.3,196.96],[196.96,197.33],[197.33,197.55],[197.55,197.92],[197.92,198.07],[198.07,198.8]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Un informe de 2018 del Urban Indian Health Institute señaló que, de 5,712 casos de mujeres y niñas indígenas desaparecidas reportados a la base de datos del FBI en 2016, solo 116 figuraban en la base de datos federal de personas desaparecidas.","start":199.55,"end":219.72,"words":[[199.58,199.73],[199.73,200.25],[200.25,200.4],[200.4,201.6],[201.6,201.82],[201.82,202.19],[202.19,202.64],[202.64,202.94],[202.94,203.61],[203.61,204.06],[204.06,204.28],[204.54,204.69],[204.69,206.48],[206.48,206.85],[206.85,207.0],[207.0,207.52],[207.52,207.6],[207.6,207.97],[207.97,208.64],[208.64,209.61],[209.61,210.36],[210.36,210.43],[210.43,210.58],[210.58,210.88],[210.88,211.03],[211.03,211.4],[211.4,211.63],[211.63,212.07],[212.07,212.22],[212.22,213.42],[213.68,213.97],[213.97,215.09],[215.09,215.76],[215.76,215.91],[215.91,216.06],[216.06,216.36],[216.36,216.51],[216.51,216.88],[216.88,217.4],[217.4,217.55],[217.55,218.15],[218.15,219.19]]},{"el":"s2","text":"En 2020, el Congreso aprobó la Ley Savanna y la Ley Not Invisible para mejorar el seguimiento y la investigación de estos casos.","start":220.07,"end":229.0,"words":[[220.09,220.24],[220.24,221.19],[221.44,221.59],[221.59,222.18],[222.18,222.62],[222.62,222.76],[222.76,222.98],[222.98,223.5],[223.5,223.57],[223.57,223.71],[223.71,223.93],[223.93,224.15],[224.15,224.81],[224.81,225.11],[225.11,225.62],[225.62,225.77],[225.77,226.5],[226.5,226.57],[226.57,226.72],[226.72,227.67],[227.67,227.82],[227.82,228.18],[228.18,228.62]]},{"el":"h3","text":"La violencia policial en distintos grupos","start":229.9,"end":233.02,"words":[[229.9,230.06],[230.06,230.81],[230.81,231.47],[231.47,231.64],[231.64,232.38],[232.38,232.88]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Algunos análisis de las muertes a manos de la policía, ajustados por población, sitúan a los indígenas americanos en el primer lugar o cerca, seguidos por los estadounidenses negros; otros los ordenan distinto.","start":233.72,"end":246.62,"words":[[233.76,234.22],[234.22,234.74],[234.74,234.87],[234.87,235.07],[235.07,235.52],[235.52,235.59],[235.59,235.91],[235.91,236.05],[236.05,236.18],[236.18,236.76],[236.99,237.58],[237.58,237.78],[237.78,238.43],[238.66,239.05],[239.05,239.11],[239.11,239.31],[239.31,239.9],[239.9,240.55],[240.55,240.68],[240.68,240.81],[240.81,241.2],[241.2,241.53],[241.53,241.59],[241.59,241.99],[242.21,242.67],[242.67,242.87],[242.87,243.06],[243.06,244.04],[244.04,244.5],[244.73,245.05],[245.05,245.25],[245.25,245.71],[245.71,246.29]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Las cifras son inciertas porque la raza de las víctimas indígenas y latinas a menudo se registra mal.","start":246.97,"end":253.56,"words":[[247.02,247.24],[247.24,247.68],[247.68,247.9],[247.9,248.56],[248.56,248.93],[248.93,249.08],[249.08,249.37],[249.37,249.52],[249.52,249.74],[249.74,250.32],[250.32,250.99],[250.99,251.06],[251.06,251.57],[251.57,251.65],[251.65,252.09],[252.09,252.24],[252.24,252.82],[252.82,253.12]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La capa de muertes a manos de la policía del mapa (Mapping Police Violence) colorea cada caso según la raza de la víctima para que veas el patrón por tu cuenta.","start":253.91,"end":263.84,"words":[[253.93,254.08],[254.08,254.37],[254.37,254.52],[254.52,255.03],[255.03,255.1],[255.1,255.47],[255.47,255.62],[255.62,255.76],[255.76,256.35],[256.35,256.57],[256.57,256.86],[256.86,257.3],[257.3,257.74],[257.74,258.32],[258.58,259.09],[259.09,259.38],[259.38,259.67],[259.67,260.04],[260.04,260.18],[260.18,260.48],[260.48,260.62],[260.62,260.77],[260.77,261.28],[261.28,261.57],[261.57,261.72],[261.72,262.01],[262.01,262.16],[262.16,262.6],[262.6,262.82],[262.82,262.96],[262.96,263.48]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Unidos","start":264.74,"end":265.97,"words":[[264.76,265.74]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Frederick Douglass habló contra la exclusión china en su discurso “Nación compuesta” de 1869.","start":266.67,"end":273.82,"words":[[266.68,267.21],[267.21,267.75],[267.75,268.01],[268.01,268.41],[268.41,268.55],[268.55,269.21],[269.21,269.54],[269.54,269.68],[269.68,269.81],[269.81,270.34],[270.34,270.74],[270.74,271.34],[271.34,271.48],[271.48,273.34]]},{"el":"s4","text":"En 1965, trabajadores agrícolas filipinos encabezados por Larry Itliong iniciaron la huelga de la uva de Delano y pidieron al sindicato mexicoamericano de César Chávez que se uniera; juntos lograron los primeros grandes contratos para trabajadores agrícolas.","start":274.17,"end":293.1,"words":[[274.19,274.34],[274.34,276.43],[276.69,277.58],[277.58,278.25],[278.25,278.92],[278.92,279.74],[279.74,279.96],[279.96,280.26],[280.26,280.78],[280.78,281.45],[281.45,281.6],[281.6,281.97],[281.97,282.12],[282.12,282.27],[282.27,282.49],[282.49,282.64],[282.64,283.09],[283.09,283.16],[283.16,283.76],[283.76,283.91],[283.91,284.58],[284.58,285.69],[285.69,285.84],[285.84,286.21],[286.21,286.66],[286.66,286.81],[286.81,286.96],[286.96,287.48],[287.74,288.19],[288.19,288.78],[288.78,289.01],[289.01,289.6],[289.6,290.12],[290.12,290.79],[290.79,291.09],[291.09,291.98],[291.98,292.73]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La activista japonesa-estadounidense Yuri Kochiyama trabajó junto a Malcolm X y estaba con él cuando lo mataron.","start":293.45,"end":301.54,"words":[[293.45,293.6],[293.6,294.31],[294.31,296.03],[296.03,296.35],[296.35,297.05],[297.05,297.6],[297.6,297.99],[297.99,298.07],[298.07,298.62],[298.62,298.93],[298.93,299.01],[299.01,299.48],[299.48,299.72],[299.72,299.87],[299.87,300.34],[300.34,300.5],[300.5,301.13]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Organizadores negros, latinos, asiáticos e indígenas trabajaron juntos en las décadas de 1960 y 1970, y la Ley CAREN los protege a todos.","start":301.89,"end":313.28,"words":[[301.89,302.78],[302.78,303.26],[303.5,304.05],[304.29,304.9],[304.9,304.97],[304.97,305.59],[305.59,306.28],[306.28,306.69],[306.69,306.82],[306.82,307.03],[307.03,307.51],[307.51,307.65],[307.65,309.09],[309.09,309.15],[309.15,310.66],[310.9,310.97],[310.97,311.11],[311.11,311.31],[311.31,311.66],[311.66,311.86],[311.86,312.34],[312.34,312.41],[312.41,312.82]]}],"audio":"https://carenactmedia.blob.core.windows.net/audio/es/many-targets.male.902b429146.mp3","bytes":1257012,"sha256":"902b429146a2e4aae14e8003dfc1043d5cdc278ed0788c55adf00a51fce5326f"}